        [yin.vm.data :as data]\n             [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\n@@ -1235,4 +1241,266 @@\n           \":a/publisher and :b/publisher stay distinct (namespace kept)\")\n       (is (not= (get-in res-a [:call-sites :origin])\n                 (get-in res-s [:call-sites :origin]))\n-          \"the keyword and the string of the same name stay distinct\"))))\n\\ No newline at end of file\n+          \"the keyword and the string of the same name stay distinct\"))))\n+\n+\n+;; =============================================================================\n+;; cc2: transform & session C1 preservation\n+;; =============================================================================\n+\n+(defn- sp-var\n+  [s]\n+  {:type :variable :name s})\n+\n+\n+(defn- sp-app\n+  [op & args]\n+  {:type :application :operator op :operands (vec args)})\n+\n+\n+(defn- sp-lam\n+  [params body]\n+  {:type :lambda :params params :body body})\n+\n+\n+(def ^:private sp-ast\n+  \"`((fn [w] (w w)) (fn [w] (f w)))`, both lambdas site-marked (`:call`,\n+   `:loop`) and every application C1-marked, tails marked as a frontend\n+   would.\"\n+  (yang/annotate-call-sites\n+    (tails/mark-tails\n+      (sp-app (vary-meta (sp-lam '[w] (sp-app (sp-var 'w) (sp-var 'w)))\n+                         assoc :yang/site :call)\n+              (vary-meta (sp-lam '[w] (sp-app (sp-var 'f) (sp-var 'w)))\n+                         assoc :yang/site :loop)))))\n+\n+\n+(def ^:private sp-profile {:loop 'h/loop :call 'h/call})\n+(def ^:private sp-origin (vm/source-origin :m [:t 0] 0))\n+(def ^:private sp-injected-origin [:source :test/publication \"safepoint-c1\" 0])\n+\n+\n+(defn- sp-projected\n+  [ast]\n+  (encoder/project (encoder/source-envelope :m [:t 0] [ast])))\n+\n+\n+(defn- entry-set\n+  [correspondence kind]\n+  (into #{} (filter #(= kind (:kind %))) (:entries correspondence)))\n+\n+\n+(deftest safepoint-c1-preservation-test\n+  (let [input (sp-projected sp-ast)\n+        input-tree (first (:yin/batch input))\n+        input-rows (filterv #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3))\n+                            (:yin/frontend-metadata input))]\n+    (is (seq input-rows) \"the input envelope carries a C1 claim\")\n+    (testing \"without a supplied injected origin, surviving occurrences\n+              keep their own origin at their shifted paths and injected\n+              occurrences are identified but unclaimed\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yang/safepoint.cljc | sed -n '1,470p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yang.safepoint\n     2\t  \"The safepoint stage (Architect safepoint-interpreter design, slice 1): a\n     3\t   pure rewrite of a canonical program tree `A` into a derived tree `A'` that\n     4\t   applies a hook at every frontend-marked site the profile maps.\n     5\t   Language-neutral: it knows the Universal AST row grammar and the\n     6\t   frontend-metadata side table, nothing about any guest language. The hooks'\n     7\t   meaning lives in a per-language hook prelude; the evaluator never learns\n     8\t   what a safepoint is.\n     9\t\n    10\t   - A site is a `:lambda` occurrence the frontend marked with `:yang/site`\n    11\t     metadata, which projection puts in the side table as\n    12\t     `[origin root path :yang/site kind]`. A profile `{kind hook-symbol}`\n    13\t     selects sites; a kind it omits is not inserted.\n    14\t   - Insertion prefixes the site's body with an ordinary `:application` of\n    15\t     the hook, sequenced through a lambda whose one binder is `binder`, in a\n    16\t     reserved namespace: no new tag, no gensym counter. An exit kind\n    17\t     (`exit-kinds`: `:return` at `:call` sites) wraps the body instead: its\n    18\t     hook is applied to the body's value, so it runs on normal exit only.\n    19\t   - A mark's value is a kind, or a vector `[kind datum ...]`: the data\n    20\t     (a function's name and line, a statement's line) are literals the\n    21\t     frontend knows and the derived tree may need. A profile entry is a\n    22\t     hook symbol, or `{:hook symbol :operands true}` to apply the hook to\n    23\t     the mark's data. A statement kind (`statement-kinds`: `:line`) marks\n    24\t     any node, not a lambda; its hook is applied before the node, which\n    25\t     is sequenced after it.\n    26\t   - Every tail mark is stripped and recomputed over the whole derived tree\n    27\t     (`yang.tails`): a wrapped body's old tail calls would otherwise skip\n    28\t     its wrapper. With no site selected `A'` is `A`, row for row.\n    29\t   - `A` is never modified. Names, the ledger and publication refer to it;\n    30\t     the link is a `:derive` record with input `A`, output `A'`, function\n    31\t     `function`, and a profile pinning the hook map and the address of the\n    32\t     sorted site set. Insertion is deterministic, so a repeat writes the\n    33\t     same record.\n    34\t   - `A'` leaves on the stage's own medium in a projected envelope whose\n    35\t     batch token is the record's address, so its occurrence origin is an\n    36\t     ordinary `[:source medium' token 0]`. No side table is copied: an `A'`\n    37\t     node's facts are a join back to `A` through the site set. The one\n    38\t     exception is the C1 claim: when the input claims `:yang/call-site`\n    39\t     coverage, `derive-envelope` recomputes its rows over `A'` (never\n    40\t     copies them — paths shift) and records the input→output occurrence\n    41\t     correspondence as data.\"\n    42\t  (:require\n    43\t    [dao.jing :as jing]\n    44\t    [yang.stage :as stage]\n    45\t    [yang.tails :as tails]\n    46\t    [yin.vm :as vm]))\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\t(def binder\n    50\t  \"The parameter of every inserted sequencing lambda.\"\n    51\t  'yang.safepoint/_)\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\t(def function\n    55\t  \"The `:yin.ledger/function` of a safepoint derivation.\"\n    56\t  :yang.safepoint/insert)\n    57\t\n    58\t\n    59\t(def site-key\n    60\t  \"The frontend-metadata key a site mark travels under.\"\n    61\t  :yang/site)\n    62\t\n    63\t\n    64\t(def call-site-key\n    65\t  \"The frontend-metadata key of the call-site occurrence contract C1,\n    66\t   recomputed over a derived tree beside the safepoint site marks.\"\n    67\t  :yang/call-site)\n    68\t\n    69\t\n    70\t(defn sites\n    71\t  \"`{path mark}` (a kind, or `[kind datum ...]`) of every site marked in the frontend-metadata relation\n    72\t   `metadata` at occurrence `origin` of tree `root`.\"\n    73\t  [metadata origin root]\n    74\t  (into {}\n    75\t        (keep (fn [[o r path k v]]\n    76\t                (when (and (= o origin) (= r root) (= k site-key))\n    77\t                  [path v])))\n    78\t        metadata))\n    79\t\n    80\t\n    81\t(defn site-set\n    82\t  \"The selected sites as a sorted vector of `[path mark]`, a mark a kind or `[kind datum ...]`, in an order every\n    83\t   host computes alike.\"\n    84\t  [selected]\n    85\t  (vec (sort-by pr-str (map vec selected))))\n    86\t\n    87\t\n    88\t(def exit-kinds\n    89\t  \"Exit kind -> the entry kind whose sites it wraps. An exit hook is applied\n    90\t   to the value of the site's body, so it runs after a normal exit and its\n    91\t   answer is the body's value; an escape out of the body skips it.\"\n    92\t  {:return :call})\n    93\t\n    94\t\n    95\t(def statement-kinds\n    96\t  \"Kinds whose sites are any node, not a lambda: the hook runs before the\n    97\t   node, and the node's value is the site's.\"\n    98\t  #{:line})\n    99\t\n   100\t\n   101\t(defn- mark-kind\n   102\t  [mark]\n   103\t  (if (vector? mark) (first mark) mark))\n   104\t\n   105\t\n   106\t(defn- entry-hook\n   107\t  \"The `{:hook sym :operands [literal ...]}` of profile entry `entry` at a\n   108\t   site marked `mark`, or nil.\"\n   109\t  [entry mark]\n   110\t  (when entry\n   111\t    (if (map? entry)\n   112\t      {:hook (:hook entry),\n   113\t       :operands (when (:operands entry) (vec (rest mark)))}\n   114\t      {:hook entry})))\n   115\t\n   116\t\n   117\t(defn- site-hooks\n   118\t  \"`{:enter h :exit h}` (either absent), each an `entry-hook`, for a site\n   119\t   marked `mark` under `profile`.\"\n   120\t  [profile mark]\n   121\t  (let [kind (mark-kind mark)\n   122\t        exit (some (fn [[x entry]] (when (= entry kind) (get profile x)))\n   123\t                   exit-kinds)]\n   124\t    (cond-> {}\n   125\t      (get profile kind) (assoc :enter (entry-hook (get profile kind) mark))\n   126\t      (and (map? (get profile kind)) (:sequence (get profile kind)))\n   127\t      (assoc :sequence? true)\n   128\t      exit (assoc :exit (entry-hook exit mark)))))\n   129\t\n   130\t\n   131\t(defn- hook-application\n   132\t  [{:keys [hook operands]} args]\n   133\t  {:type :application,\n   134\t   :operator {:type :variable, :name hook},\n   135\t   :operands (into (mapv (fn [x] {:type :literal, :value x}) operands) args)})\n   136\t\n   137\t\n   138\t(defn- sequence-hook\n   139\t  \"`node` evaluated after `hook` is applied.\"\n   140\t  [node hook]\n   141\t  {:type :application,\n   142\t   :operator {:type :lambda, :params [binder], :body node},\n   143\t   :operands [(hook-application hook [])]})\n   144\t\n   145\t\n   146\t(defn- prefix-hook\n   147\t  \"Lambda `node` with `hook` applied before its body runs.\"\n   148\t  [node hook]\n   149\t  (assoc node\n   150\t         :body (sequence-hook (:body node) hook)))\n   151\t\n   152\t\n   153\t(defn- wrap-hook\n   154\t  \"Lambda `node` with `hook` applied to its body's value.\"\n   155\t  [node hook]\n   156\t  (assoc node :body (hook-application hook [(:body node)])))\n   157\t\n   158\t\n   159\t(defn- rewrite\n   160\t  \"The map AST `ast` with each `{path {:enter h :exit h}}` site's exit hook\n   161\t   wrapped around its body and its entry hook prefixed. Throws when a site\n   162\t   names no node, or a node that is not a lambda.\"\n   163\t  [ast hooks]\n   164\t  (let [seen (volatile! #{})]\n   165\t    (letfn [(walk\n   166\t              [node path]\n   167\t              (let [slots (get vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar (:type node))\n   168\t                    node (reduce\n   169\t                           (fn [n [j [field kind]]]\n   170\t                             (let [pos (+ j 2)]\n   171\t                               (case kind\n   172\t                                 :node (update n field walk (conj path pos))\n   173\t                                 :nodes (update n field\n   174\t                                                (fn [children]\n   175\t                                                  (vec (map-indexed\n   176\t                                                         (fn [i child]\n   177\t                                                           (walk child (conj path [pos i])))\n   178\t                                                         children))))\n   179\t                                 n)))\n   180\t                           node\n   181\t                           (map-indexed vector slots))]\n   182\t                (if-let [{:keys [enter exit statement? sequence?]} (get hooks path)]\n   183\t                  (do (vswap! seen conj path)\n   184\t                      (if (or statement? sequence?)\n   185\t                        (sequence-hook node enter)\n   186\t                        (do (when-not (= :lambda (:type node))\n   187\t                              (throw (ex-info \"Safepoint site is not a lambda\"\n   188\t                                              {:rule :site-not-lambda, :path path,\n   189\t                                               :type (:type node)})))\n   190\t                            (cond-> node\n   191\t                              exit (wrap-hook exit)\n   192\t                              enter (prefix-hook enter)))))\n   193\t                  node)))]\n   194\t      (let [out (walk ast [])\n   195\t            missing (remove @seen (keys hooks))]\n   196\t        (when (seq missing)\n   197\t          (throw (ex-info \"Safepoint site names no node\"\n   198\t                          {:rule :site-missing, :paths (vec (sort-by pr-str missing))})))\n   199\t        out))))\n   200\t\n   201\t\n   202\t(defn- selected-hooks\n   203\t  \"`{path {:enter h :exit h}}` of the sites `profile` selects.\"\n   204\t  [sites profile]\n   205\t  (into {}\n   206\t        (keep (fn [[path mark]]\n   207\t                (let [h (site-hooks profile mark)]\n   208\t                  (when (seq h)\n   209\t                    [path (cond-> h\n   210\t                            (contains? statement-kinds (mark-kind mark))\n   211\t                            (assoc :statement? true))]))))\n   212\t        sites))\n   213\t\n   214\t\n   215\t(defn insert\n   216\t  \"Pure: the canonical row set `tree` (`{:root id :rows {id row}}`) with\n   217\t   each of `sites` (`{path mark}`, a mark a kind or `[kind datum ...]`) that\n   218\t   `profile` (`{kind hook}`, a hook a symbol or `{:hook sym :operands true}`)\n   219\t   maps a hook to, by its kind or by an exit kind of it, rewritten: the entry hook\n   220\t   prefixed, the exit hook wrapped around the body. Returns\n   221\t   `{:tree A' :sites selected}`. With nothing selected `A'` is `tree`\n   222\t   itself.\"\n   223\t  [tree sites profile]\n   224\t  (let [hooks (selected-hooks sites profile)\n   225\t        selected (into {}\n   226\t                       (filter (fn [[path _]] (contains? hooks path)))\n   227\t                       sites)]\n   228\t    {:tree (if (empty? hooks)\n   229\t             tree\n   230\t             (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode\n   231\t               (tails/remark-tails\n   232\t                 (rewrite (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast tree) hooks))))\n   233\t     :sites selected}))\n   234\t\n   235\t\n   236\t(defn- track-occurrences\n   237\t  \"Path arithmetic over the input map AST `ast` under the selected\n   238\t   `hooks`: `{:surviving {in-path out-path} :injected #{out-path}}` for\n   239\t   every `:application` occurrence. Wrapping never drops, duplicates, or\n   240\t   reorders a subtree — it only prefixes hook applications — so each\n   241\t   input application has exactly one output place, derived here from\n   242\t   the rewrite's own insertions, never matched by content. A sequencing\n   243\t   insertion (`sequence-hook`) puts its node under `[2 3]` beneath the\n   244\t   injected sequencing application; a lambda site's body shifts under\n   245\t   the entry sequencing application and the exit hook application.\"\n   246\t  [ast hooks]\n   247\t  (let [surviving (atom {})\n   248\t        injected (atom #{})]\n   249\t    (letfn [(walk2\n   250\t                [node in-path out-path]\n   251\t                (let [site (get hooks in-path)]\n   252\t                  (cond\n   253\t                    (and site (or (:statement? site) (:sequence? site)))\n   254\t                    (do (swap! injected conj out-path (conj out-path [3 0]))\n   255\t                        (walk-self2 node in-path (conj out-path 2 3)))\n   256\t\n   257\t                    (and site (= :lambda (:type node)))\n   258\t                    (let [{:keys [enter exit]} site\n   259\t                          body-out (into out-path\n   260\t                                         (cond\n   261\t                                           (and enter exit) [3 2 3 [3 0]]\n   262\t                                           enter [3 2 3]\n   263\t                                           exit [3 [3 0]]\n   264\t                                           :else [3]))]\n   265\t                      (when enter\n   266\t                        (swap! injected conj (conj out-path 3)\n   267\t                               (into out-path [3 [3 0]])))\n   268\t                      (when exit\n   269\t                        (swap! injected conj\n   270\t                               (if enter (conj out-path 3 2 3) (conj out-path 3))))\n   271\t                      (walk2 (:body node) (conj in-path 3) body-out))\n   272\t\n   273\t                    :else (walk-self2 node in-path out-path))))\n   274\t              (walk-self2\n   275\t                [node in-path out-path]\n   276\t                (when (= :application (:type node))\n   277\t                  (swap! surviving assoc in-path out-path))\n   278\t                (doseq [[j [field kind]] (map-indexed vector\n   279\t                                                      (get vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar\n   280\t                                                           (:type node)))\n   281\t                        :let [pos (+ j 2)\n   282\t                              value (get node field)]]\n   283\t                  (case kind\n   284\t                    :node (walk2 value (conj in-path pos) (conj out-path pos))\n   285\t                    :nodes (doseq [[i child] (map-indexed vector (or value []))]\n   286\t                             (walk2 child (conj in-path [pos i])\n   287\t                                    (conj out-path [pos i])))\n   288\t                    nil)))]\n   289\t        (walk2 ast [] []))\n   290\t      {:surviving @surviving :injected @injected}))\n   291\t\n   292\t\n   293\t(defn- derive-call-sites\n   294\t  \"Recompute the C1 rows of the derived tree from the input tree's own\n   295\t   rows: `{:metadata rows :correspondence c}`, or nil when the input\n   296\t   carries no C1 claim for `tree`. A surviving occurrence keeps its\n   297\t   input row's origin at its tracked output path. An injected\n   298\t   occurrence is claimed only under `injected-origin`, the admission\n   299\t   origin the caller supplies; without one it is recorded as injected\n   300\t   and left unclaimed. An input row whose occurrence is claimed by two\n   301\t   origins, or that names no application occurrence of the input tree,\n   302\t   is refused attribution (`:unmapped`) — never guessed.\"\n   303\t  [frontend-metadata tree derived hooks injected-origin]\n   304\t  (let [rows (filterv (fn [row]\n   305\t                        (and (sequential? row) (= 5 (count row))\n   306\t                             (= (:root tree) (nth row 1))\n   307\t                             (= call-site-key (nth row 3))))\n   308\t                      frontend-metadata)]\n   309\t    (when (seq rows)\n   310\t      (let [{:keys [surviving injected]}\n   311\t            (track-occurrences (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast tree) hooks)\n   312\t            eligible (into #{} (map second) (vm/application-occurrences tree))\n   313\t            by-path (group-by #(nth % 2) rows)\n   314\t            sorted (fn [xs] (vec (sort-by pr-str xs)))\n   315\t            parts (reduce\n   316\t                    (fn [acc [path rs]]\n   317\t                      (let [origins (distinct (map first rs))]\n   318\t                        (cond\n   319\t                          (< 1 (count origins))\n   320\t                          (update acc :unmapped into\n   321\t                                  (map (fn [o]\n   322\t                                         {:kind :unmapped\n   323\t                                          :input [o (:root tree) path]\n   324\t                                          :reason :ambiguous})\n   325\t                                       origins))\n   326\t\n   327\t                          (not (contains? eligible path))\n   328\t                          (update acc :unmapped conj\n   329\t                                  {:kind :unmapped\n   330\t                                   :input [(first (first rs)) (:root tree) path]\n   331\t                                   :reason :no-such-occurrence})\n   332\t\n   333\t                          :else\n   334\t                          (let [o (first (first rs))\n   335\t                                out (get surviving path)]\n   336\t                            (-> acc\n   337\t                                (update :entries conj\n   338\t                                        {:kind :surviving\n   339\t                                         :input [o (:root tree) path]\n   340\t                                         :output [o (:root derived) out]})\n   341\t                                (update :rows into\n   342\t                                        (map (fn [r]\n   343\t                                               [o (:root derived) out\n   344\t                                                call-site-key (nth r 4)])\n   345\t                                             rs)))))))\n   346\t                    {:entries [] :rows [] :unmapped []}\n   347\t                    (sort-by (comp pr-str key) by-path))\n   348\t            injected-entries (map (fn [p]\n   349\t                                    (cond-> {:kind :safepoint/injected :path p}\n   350\t                                      injected-origin\n   351\t                                      (assoc :origin injected-origin)))\n   352\t                                  (sorted injected))\n   353\t            injected-rows (when injected-origin\n   354\t                            (map (fn [p]\n   355\t                                   [injected-origin (:root derived) p\n   356\t                                    call-site-key 1])\n   357\t                                 injected))]\n   358\t        {:metadata (vec (sort jing/canonical-compare\n   359\t                              (distinct (into (:rows parts) injected-rows))))\n   360\t         :correspondence {:input-root (:root tree)\n   361\t                          :output-root (:root derived)\n   362\t                          :entries (into (sorted (:entries parts))\n   363\t                                         (into injected-entries\n   364\t                                               (sorted (:unmapped parts))))}}))))\n   365\t\n   366\t\n   367\t(defn derive-record\n   368\t  \"The `:derive` record linking canonical root `input` to derived root\n   369\t   `output`: function `function`, profile pinning the hook map and the\n   370\t   address of the sorted site set.\"\n   371\t  [input output profile selected]\n   372\t  {:yin.ledger/op :derive,\n   373\t   :yin.ledger/input input,\n   374\t   :yin.ledger/output output,\n   375\t   :yin.ledger/function function,\n   376\t   :yin.ledger/profile {:yang.safepoint/hooks profile,\n   377\t                        :yang.safepoint/sites (jing/segment-key\n   378\t                                                (site-set selected))}})\n   379\t\n   380\t\n   381\t(defn derive-envelope\n   382\t  \"One projected envelope from the row medium to the derived one:\n   383\t   `{:envelope e' :record r :record-address a}`. The run member of the input\n   384\t   is `A`; `e'` carries `A'` alone, on `medium`, with token `a`.\n   385\t\n   386\t   When the input envelope's frontend-metadata claims C1 for the run\n   387\t   member, `e'` carries the recomputed rows of `A'` and the answer\n   388\t   carries `:correspondence`, the explicit input→output occurrence\n   389\t   correspondence (also on `e'` as `:yang.safepoint/correspondence`).\n   390\t   `opts` may supply `:injected-origin`, the caller's admission origin\n   391\t   for the injected hook applications; without one they stay\n   392\t   unclaimed. No origin is ever derived from the trees' structure.\"\n   393\t  ([envelope profile medium]\n   394\t   (derive-envelope envelope profile medium nil))\n   395\t  ([envelope profile medium {:keys [injected-origin]}]\n   396\t   (when (and injected-origin (not (vm/occurrence-origin? injected-origin)))\n   397\t     (throw (ex-info \"Malformed injected call-site origin\"\n   398\t                     {:rule :origin, :origin injected-origin})))\n   399\t   (let [{:yin/keys [source-medium batch-token batch root frontend-metadata]}\n   400\t         envelope\n   401\t         tree (nth batch root)\n   402\t         origin (vm/source-origin source-medium batch-token root)\n   403\t         input-sites (sites frontend-metadata origin (:root tree))\n   404\t         {derived :tree selected :sites}\n   405\t         (insert tree input-sites profile)\n   406\t         {:keys [metadata correspondence]}\n   407\t         (derive-call-sites frontend-metadata tree derived\n   408\t                            (selected-hooks input-sites profile)\n   409\t                            injected-origin)\n   410\t         record (derive-record (:root tree) (:root derived) profile selected)\n   411\t         address (jing/segment-key record)]\n   412\t     (vm/source-origin medium address 0)\n   413\t     (cond-> {:envelope (cond-> {:yin/source-medium medium,\n   414\t                                 :yin/batch-token address,\n   415\t                                 :yin/batch [derived],\n   416\t                                 :yin/root 0,\n   417\t                                 :yin/source-positions [],\n   418\t                                 :yin/frontend-metadata (or metadata []),\n   419\t                                 :yin/entity-occurrences []}\n   420\t                          correspondence\n   421\t                          (assoc :yang.safepoint/correspondence correspondence)),\n   422\t              :record record,\n   423\t              :record-address address}\n   424\t       correspondence (assoc :correspondence correspondence)))))\n   425\t\n   426\t\n   427\t(defn transform\n   428\t  \"The stage's transform over projected envelopes: `A'` on port `:program`,\n   429\t   its `:derive` record on port `:ledger`. State is `{:profile p :medium m}`\n   430\t   and never changes.\"\n   431\t  [{:keys [profile medium], :as state} envelope]\n   432\t  (let [{:keys [envelope record]} (derive-envelope envelope profile medium)]\n   433\t    [state [[:program envelope] [:ledger record]]]))\n   434\t\n   435\t\n   436\t(defn open-stage\n   437\t  \"A safepoint stage reading projected envelopes from `rows`, writing derived\n   438\t   envelopes to `program` (logical identity `medium`) and records to\n   439\t   `ledger`.\"\n   440\t  [rows program ledger profile medium]\n   441\t  (stage/open rows\n   442\t              {:program program, :ledger ledger}\n   443\t              {:profile profile, :medium medium}))\n   444\t\n   445\t\n   446\t(defn step-stage\n   447\t  [s]\n   448\t  (stage/step s transform))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '580,820p' /tmp/cc2-review-diff.txt; rg --files -g AGENTS.md; rg -n '\"'^### 2.[24]|''^## 2|''^### 2'\"' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md\"","aggregated_output":"+              occurrences are identified but unclaimed\"\n+      (let [{:keys [envelope correspondence]}\n+            (safepoint/derive-envelope input sp-profile :m')\n+            derived-tree (first (:yin/batch envelope))\n+            md (:yin/frontend-metadata envelope)\n+            surviving (entry-set correspondence :surviving)\n+            injected (entry-set correspondence :safepoint/injected)]\n+        (is (some? correspondence))\n+        (is (= (count input-rows) (count surviving))\n+            \"every claimed input occurrence survives (wrapping never drops one)\")\n+        (is (= (into #{} (map :input) surviving)\n+               (into #{} (map #(vec (take 3 %))) input-rows))\n+            \"the correspondence names every claimed input occurrence\")\n+        (is (= (into #{} (map :output) surviving) (marked md))\n+            \"the derived rows are exactly the surviving occurrences\")\n+        (is (= #{sp-origin} (row-origins md))\n+            \"surviving rows keep the input rows' own origin, none fabricated\")\n+        (is (seq injected) \"the hook insertions are recorded as injected\")\n+        (is (every? #(not (contains? % :origin)) injected)\n+            \"with no origin supplied by the caller, none is invented\")\n+        (is (= (into #{} (map (fn [e] [(:root derived-tree) (:path e)])) injected)\n+               (into #{} (remove (into #{}\n+                                       (map (fn [[_ r p]] [r p])\n+                                            (map :output surviving)))\n+                                 (occurrence-pairs derived-tree))))\n+            \"the unclaimed derived occurrences are exactly the injected ones\")\n+        (testing \"canonical invariance: C1 carriage changes no row or root\"\n+          (let [plain (safepoint/derive-envelope\n+                        (sp-projected (strip-call-sites sp-ast))\n+                        sp-profile :m')]\n+            (is (= (:root derived-tree)\n+                   (:root (first (:yin/batch (:envelope plain))))))\n+            (is (= derived-tree (first (:yin/batch (:envelope plain)))))))))\n+    (testing \"with a caller-supplied admission origin, the derived table\n+              covers the derived tree completely and the injected rows\n+              carry that origin alone\"\n+      (let [{:keys [envelope correspondence]}\n+            (safepoint/derive-envelope input sp-profile :m'\n+                                       {:injected-origin sp-injected-origin})\n+            derived-tree (first (:yin/batch envelope))\n+            md (:yin/frontend-metadata envelope)\n+            surviving (entry-set correspondence :surviving)\n+            injected (entry-set correspondence :safepoint/injected)]\n+        (is (= (occurrence-pairs derived-tree) (marked-pairs md))\n+            \"the recomputed table covers every derived application\")\n+        (is (true? (yang/validate-call-site-coverage!\n+                     derived-tree md sp-injected-origin\n+                     {:declared? true :per-occurrence-origins? true})))\n+        (is (every? #(= sp-injected-origin (:origin %)) injected))\n+        (is (= (into #{} (map (fn [e] [(:origin e) (:root derived-tree) (:path e)]))\n+                     injected)\n+               (into #{} (filter #(= sp-injected-origin (first %))) (marked md)))\n+            \"the injected rows are exactly the injected correspondence entries\")\n+        (is (= (into #{} (map :output) surviving)\n+               (into #{} (filter #(= sp-origin (first %))) (marked md)))\n+            \"the surviving rows keep the input origin\")))\n+    (testing \"an ambiguous or stale input row is refused attribution,\n+              never guessed\"\n+      (let [victim (first input-rows)\n+            other-origin [:source :other-publisher \"batch-9\" 0]\n+            bad (assoc input :yin/frontend-metadata\n+                       (into (:yin/frontend-metadata input)\n+                             [[other-origin (nth victim 1) (nth victim 2)\n+                               :yang/call-site 1]\n+                              [sp-origin (:root input-tree) [99]\n+                               :yang/call-site 1]]))\n+            {:keys [envelope correspondence]}\n+            (safepoint/derive-envelope bad sp-profile :m'\n+                                       {:injected-origin sp-injected-origin})\n+            unmapped (entry-set correspondence :unmapped)]\n+        (is (= #{(vec (take 3 victim))\n+                 [other-origin (nth victim 1) (nth victim 2)]\n+                 [sp-origin (:root input-tree) [99]]}\n+               (into #{} (map :input) unmapped))\n+            \"both claims on the double-claimed occurrence and the stale\n+             occurrence are unmapped\")\n+        (is (not (contains? (marked (:yin/frontend-metadata envelope))\n+                            (some #(when (= (vec (take 3 victim)) (:input %))\n+                                     (:output %))\n+                                  (entry-set correspondence :surviving))))\n+            \"no surviving row is emitted for the refused occurrence\")))))\n+\n+\n+(deftest encoder-projected-member-test\n+  (testing \"an already-projected {:root :rows} member keeps the\n+            frontend-metadata its caller supplied, validated like a\n+            map-AST member's claim\"\n+    (let [ast (yang/compile '(+ (* 2 3) 4))\n+          tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)\n+          tables (vm/ast-side-tables ast tree origin)\n+          member (assoc tree :frontend-metadata (:frontend-metadata tables)\n+                             :source-positions (:source-positions tables))\n+          projected (encoder/project\n+                      (encoder/source-envelope :program \"batch-1\" [member]))]\n+      (is (= (:frontend-metadata tables) (:yin/frontend-metadata projected))\n+          \"the supplied rows survive projection verbatim\")\n+      (is (= (:root tree) (:root (first (:yin/batch projected))))\n+          \"the canonical root is untouched by the carriage\")\n+      (is (= (:rows tree) (:rows (first (:yin/batch projected))))\n+          \"the canonical rows are untouched by the carriage\")))\n+  (testing \"a broken claim on a projected member refuses projection\"\n+    (let [ast (yang/compile '(+ (* 2 3) 4))\n+          tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)\n+          tables (vm/ast-side-tables ast tree origin)\n+          rows (:frontend-metadata tables)]\n+      (is (= :yang/call-site-incomplete-coverage\n+             (failure-rule\n+               #(encoder/project\n+                  (encoder/source-envelope\n+                    :program \"batch-1\"\n+                    [(assoc tree :frontend-metadata (pop rows))])))))\n+      (is (= :yang/call-site-unsupported-version\n+             (failure-rule\n+               #(encoder/project\n+                  (encoder/source-envelope\n+                    :program \"batch-1\"\n+                    [(assoc tree :frontend-metadata\n+                            (assoc-in rows [0 4] 2))])))))))\n+  (testing \"a projected member carrying no metadata stays legacy\"\n+    (let [tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode (yang/compile '(+ 1 2)))\n+          projected (encoder/project\n+                      (encoder/source-envelope :program \"batch-1\" [tree]))]\n+      (is (= [] (:yin/frontend-metadata projected)))\n+      (is (= tree (first (:yin/batch projected)))))))\n+\n+\n+(defn- session-index\n+  \"Evaluate `lines` in a fresh REPL session; answer `{:state s :db db}`\n+   with the published index relation (as `publish_test` builds it).\"\n+  [lines]\n+  (let [state (reduce (fn [s line] (first (repl/eval-input s line)))\n+                      (repl-frontends/create-state)\n+                      lines)\n+        ix (:indexer state)]\n+    {:state state\n+     :db (query/relation\n+           (vec (space.index/read-datoms (:content-store ix)\n+                                         (:manifest-address ix))))}))\n+\n+\n+(deftest module-from-index-c1-test\n+  (let [{:keys [state db]} (session-index [\"(def k (fn [] 1))\"\n+                                           \"(def g (fn [] (+ (k) 41)))\"])\n+        tables (repl/call-site-tables state)]\n+    (is (seq tables) \"the session expander retains the executed tables\")\n+    (is (= tables (:call-site-tables (:expander state))))\n+    (testing \"with the retained tables, the recovered module claims C1\n+              and publishes its side table\"\n+      (let [spec (publish/module-from-index\n+                   db {:name 'closed :exports '[g] :primitives vm/primitives\n+                       :call-site-tables tables})\n+            store (mem/create-content-mem)\n+            res (publish/publish-module! store spec)]\n+        (is (not= :refused (:status spec)))\n+        (is (true? (yang/validate-ast-call-sites! (:ast spec) origin))\n+            \"the recovered tree's markers exactly cover its applications\")\n+        (is (jing/segment-address? (:address res)) (pr-str res))\n+        (is (some? (get-in res [:call-sites :record]))\n+            \"the publication retains the recovered claim's side table\")\n+        (let [{:keys [tree origin rows]}\n+              (publish/published-call-site-table store res)]\n+          (is (= (eligible-under tree origin) (marked rows)))\n+          (is (true? (yang/validate-call-site-coverage!\n+                       tree rows origin {:declared? true}))))))\n+    (testing \"without retained proof, the recovered tree carries no\n+              minted markers and publishes without a C1 claim\"\n+      (doseq [opts [{:name 'closed :exports '[g] :primitives vm/primitives}\n+                    {:name 'closed :exports '[g] :primitives vm/primitives\n+                     :call-site-tables {}}]]\n+        (let [spec (publish/module-from-index db opts)\n+              tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode (:ast spec))\n+              tables (vm/ast-side-tables (:ast spec) tree origin)\n+              res (publish/publish-module! (mem/create-content-mem) spec)]\n+          (is (empty? (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3))\n+                              (:frontend-metadata tables)))\n+              \"no marker is invented for an unproven recovery\")\n+          (is (jing/segment-address? (:address res)))\n+          (is (not (contains? res :call-sites))\n+              \"the publication makes no C1 claim\"))))))\n+\n+\n+(deftest repl-call-site-surface-test\n+  (testing \"render-compile-output surfaces the expansion's call sites\n+            when non-empty, and only then\"\n+    (let [store (macro/seed-store\n+                  (macro/make-ctx {:token :callsite-test/standard-forms\n+                                   :source-medium :callsite-test/standard-forms})\n+                  [macro/stdlib-forms])\n+          ctx (macro/make-ctx {:token \"callsite-test\"\n+                               :source-medium :program-in\n+                               :store store})\n+          state {:expander {:ctx ctx}}\n+          ast (yang/compile '(+ (* 2 3) 4))]\n+      (is (str/includes? (#'repl/render-compile-output state ast)\n+                         \"Call sites\")\n+          \"a claimed expansion renders its side table\")\n+      (is (not (str/includes?\n+                 (#'repl/render-compile-output state (strip-call-sites ast))\n+                 \"Call sites\"))\n+          \"an unclaimed expansion renders none\")))\n+  (testing \"the link context carries the expander's retained tables\"\n+    (let [tables {[origin :segment/root] []}]\n+      (is (= tables (:call-site-tables\n+                      (#'repl/link-context\n+                        {:expander {:call-site-tables tables}}\n+                        {:primitives {} :modules {}})))))))\n\\ No newline at end of file\nAGENTS.md\n28:## 2. Occurrence contract C1\n32:### 2.1 Identity and scope\n47:### 2.2 Minimal persisted annotation\n63:### 2.3 Finalization and transformations\n71:### 2.4 Lowering, reconstruction, and runtime lookup\n79:### 2.5 Ephemeral origin and trace field\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"I found a likely path error: the exit-hook tracker always puts the original body at operand 0, but hooks can prepend literal operands. I’m checking the affected code and whether downstream validation would catch or silently accept the wrong path."}}
