                {:rule :origin, :origin origin})))\n   970\t    origin))\n   971\t\n   972\t\n   973\t(defn loaded-code-floor\n   974\t  \"The lowest entity id claimed by the segments in a `{segment-id image}`\n   975\t   code map — each segment id minus its length — or 0 when none is loaded.\n   976\t   A loader minting a fresh local segment id allocates below this floor\n   977\t   (`semantic/load-ast` for projected AST batches, `semantic/load-vector`\n   978\t   for canonical instruction vectors), so successive loads never collide\n   979\t   with a live id.\"\n   980\t  [code]\n   981\t  (if (map? code)\n   982\t    (reduce-kv (fn [floor seg image]\n   983\t                 (if (and (integer? seg) (map? image))\n   984\t                   (min floor (- seg (or (:length image) 0)))\n   985\t                   floor))\n   986\t               0\n   987\t               code)\n   988\t    0))\n   989\t\n   990\t\n   991\t;; =============================================================================\n   992\t;; Semantic bytecode: flat content-addressed rows\n   993\t;; =============================================================================\n   994\t;; docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md §2. One row `[id tag & slots]` per\n   995\t;; distinct node; `id` is `(jing/segment-key [tag & slots])`.\n   996\t\n   997\t(def semantic-bytecode-grammar\n   998\t  \"The Universal AST row-slot table (yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md §2.3):\n   999\t   tag -> ordered `[field kind]` slots, rather than executable bytecode. Position `i` of a\n  1000\t   row body (after the tag) holds the map field named at `i`, so this one\n  1001\t   table drives both projection and reconstruction.\"\n  1002\t  {:literal [[:value :data]],\n  1003\t   :variable [[:name :sym]],\n  1004\t   :lambda [[:params :syms] [:body :node]],\n  1005\t   :application [[:operator :node] [:operands :nodes] [:tail? :bool]],\n  1006\t   :if [[:test :node] [:consequent :node] [:alternate :node]],\n  1007\t   :dao.stream.