{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-11-10 21:27:37 GMT  \nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-11 04:27:37 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\nREVIEW VERDICT: REQUEST CHANGES\n\nStatic review completed; all 17 supplied diff hunks match the actual files. No files edited or tests run.\n\n- **P0 | [safepoint.cljc:261](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yang/safepoint.cljc:261) | Exit-hook correspondence silently targets the wrong occurrence.** For a root lambda containing `(f)`, marked `[:call :tag]`, profile `{:return {:hook 'h/return :operands true}}` produces `(h/return :tag (f))`. The body application is at `[3 [3 1]]`, but tracking reports `[3 [3 0]]`, the literal. [Hook construction:135](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yang/safepoint.cljc:135) prepends literals; tracking hardcodes operand zero in both exit branches. [Derivation:335](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yang/safepoint.cljc:335) emits this as `:surviving` without checking the output occurrence. **Required fix:** calculate the body operand index from the exit hook’s operands; verify mapped output applications and refuse invalid correspondence. Cover exit-only, entry-plus-exit, and nested marks.\n\n- **P0 | [publish.cljc:568](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:568) | Recovery borrows proof across distinct admissions of identical content.** `proven-call-sites?` explicitly ignores `_origin` and accepts any table matching the root and application paths. Admission A can claim root R, followed by unclaimed admission B producing R; publishing B then accepts A’s retained table. This defeats the distinction expressly retained by [macro/call-site-table:1849](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1849). [Module assembly:694](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:694) subsequently replaces the evidence with blanket markers, retaining no old/new occurrence correspondence. **Required fix:** resolve proof using the indexed program’s actual admission plus root, refusing recovery when that association is unavailable. Preserve the selected occurrence history through assembly; claim synthesized wrappers separately under publication admission.\n\n- **P1 | [encoder.cljc:316](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc:316) | Projected claims accept malformed origins and conflicting ownership.** For a tree whose sole application is its root, `[[nil R [] :yang/call-site 1]]` passes: validation checks version and `[root path]` coverage but never origin validity. Duplicate rows, extra row fields, and two origins claiming the same application also survive because coverage is reduced to a set. [project-member:123](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc:123) then forwards them unchanged. **Required fix:** validate complete row shape, ruled origins, and unique occurrence ownership, alongside exact coverage and version.\n\n- **P1 | [repl.cljc:1317](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1317) | Normal REPL publication remains disconnected.** Tables enter `link-context`, but [query/link-answer:810](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc:810) constructs publication options without them. Consequently ordinary `yin.link/publish` still publishes claim-free. Forwarding alone also leaves custody incomplete: [dht/publish-name!:70](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/dht.cljc:70) discards `:call-sites`, whose record is deliberately undiscoverable from a bare manifest ([publish.cljc:438](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:438)). **Required fix:** complete table forwarding and retain/expose the publication side-record handle through the session path. Coordinate the necessary ownership extension.\n\n- **P2 | [clojure_callsite_test.cljc:1278](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc:1278) | The new tests miss the blocking cases.** The safepoint fixture exercises entry hooks only. Its refusal assertion at [1377](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc:1377) searches surviving correspondence for the refused input, obtains nil, and can pass even if a metadata row leaked. Index tests at [1441](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc:1441) cover valid and absent/empty tables, not stale admissions, incomplete tables, or wrong versions. **Required fix:** add those adversarial cases, invalid injected-origin coverage, and independently compute the forbidden output coordinate.\n\nRequested properties that passed static inspection:\n\n- **Publication wrapper origin is recorded, not newly fabricated by this diff:** admission selection and side-record persistence occur at [publish.cljc:279](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:279) and [358](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:358), consistent with U2.\n- **Absent injected origin produces no injected claim; ambiguous and nonexistent input paths are explicitly unmapped:** [safepoint.cljc:319](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yang/safepoint.cljc:319), [353](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yang/safepoint.cljc:353). The stage still uses the origin-free three-argument call at [432](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yang/safepoint.cljc:432).\n- **Coverage comparisons are exact equality**, and a genuinely different root cannot reuse the old table: [publish.cljc:572](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:572), [encoder.cljc:333](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc:333).\n- **Canonical separation remains intact on inspected paths:** grammar-only projection excludes node annotations ([vm.cljc:1117](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1117)); m